# The Jedi Exile the TSL chain plays (chain.flags passes it to every
# route): made by TSL's own character creation at the new game the
# prologue starts, and levelled by this plan from then on. The build is a
# light-side Jedi Sentinel made to open the most of what the story gates on
# a skill. Reader: `launcher::playthrough::build`; rules: `sim::creation`,
# `sim::levels`.

# The Sentinel has the most skill points of the three Jedi classes (3 a
# level, before Intelligence) and the most class skills that the story
# asks for (Awareness, Computer Use, Persuade, Security, Treat Injury).
class sentinel
# A man: the Handmaiden joins (the Disciple goes with a woman), as the
# walkthroughs the routes follow play it.
sex male
portrait po_pmha01
name Exile

# TSL's point-buy: 30 points from 8 in each (a point a raise to 14, two to
# 16, three to 18). Intelligence 16 (10 points) for 24 skill points at the
# first level and 6 a level after, and Computer Use, Repair and Security;
# Charisma 14 (6) for Persuade and the influence it brings; Wisdom 12 (4)
# for Awareness and Treat Injury and the Force points; Dexterity 12 (4) and
# Constitution 12 (4) for defence and vitality; Strength 10 (2), since the
# chain's fights are not what it tests (chain.flags' --mighty).
abilities 10 12 12 16 12 14

# The first level's 24 points: the five class skills the story checks at 4
# (the most a first level allows), and Repair, a cross-class skill at two
# points a rank, at its most of 2 (Peragus's and Dantooine's droids and
# terminals). Stealth and Demolitions are left at the first level.
skills computer=4 awareness=4 persuade=4 security=4 treat=4 repair=2
# The first level's one feat: Empathy, more Persuade, Awareness and Treat
# Injury.
feats EMPATHY

# Each level-up spends its points in this order, each skill to the most its
# level allows before the next: Persuade first (the most conversations and
# influence), then Awareness, Computer Use, Security, Repair (when its
# cross-class most rises, every other level) and Treat Injury, then
# Demolitions (cross-class too) for Korriban's vision of Dxun's minefield
# ("[Demolitions] Let me go first", c_sc_dem_gt: over 5) and its mines.
# What is left is kept for the next level, as TSL's level-up screen keeps
# unspent points: the odd point of a level whose Repair most did not rise
# buys the next level's rank, and none goes to Stealth (the class's order
# would put it there), which no route needs.
skill-order persuade awareness computer security repair treat demolitions
bank
# Feats as the Sentinel's levels offer them: Gear Head (Computer Use,
# Repair, Security), then each tier of Empathy and Gear Head as it opens,
# Toughness between; after these the class's recommended.
feat-order GEAR_HEAD IMPROVED_EMPATHY GEAR_HEAD_ADEPT TOUGHNESS MASTER__EMPATHY GEAR_HEAD_MASTER
# Light-side powers before the class's recommended order (which puts the
# dark Force Scream third): Burst of Speed and Force Valor to start, Cure
# as soon as the sixth level opens it, Force Push and Stun for crowds,
# Energy Resistance and Droid Stun after; then Heal, Knight's Valor and
# Speed as they open.
power-order FORCE_POWER_SPEED_BURST FORCE_POWER_FORCE_VALOR FORCE_POWER_CURE FORCE_POWER_FORCE_PUSH FORCE_POWER_STUN FORCE_POWER_RESIST_ENERGY_1 FORCE_POWER_DROID_STUN FORCE_POWER_HEAL FORCE_POWER_KNIGHT_VALOR FORCE_POWER_KNIGHT_SPEED
# Every fourth level's ability point: Intelligence twice (18 at the eighth
# level, 7 skill points a level from then), then Charisma.
raises int int cha cha cha
